            <ArticleTitle>[A toddler with nightly vomiting and pain in the abdomen].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D2069</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 4-year-old boy was referred to the emergency department with four days of nightly vomiting after ingestion of a marble. Abdominal X-ray showed the marble in the antrum of the stomach. The marble was successfully removed by endoscopy. X-rays detect 86% of all glass objects and should therefore be considered as diagnostic option by ingestion of a marble.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
